      "summaries": {
        "en": "Palmier Pro is a macOS video editor designed to integrate AI directly into the editing workflow, solving the problem of manual, time-consuming video production. Its core strength lies in leveraging local AI models like Claude and Seedance2 for tasks such as scene detection, transcription, and automated editing, all while keeping data private on-device. You can use it to quickly generate rough cuts from transcripts or apply AI-powered effects, making it ideal for content creators who want to speed up post-production without leaving the desktop.",
        "zh": "Palmier Pro 是一款专为 macOS 设计的 AI 原生视频编辑器，通过本地运行的 AI 模型（如 Claude 和 Seedance2）实现场景检测、语音转文字、自动剪辑等功能，所有数据在设备端处理，保障隐私安全。技术上采用 Swift 原生开发确保高性能，并支持 MCP 协议扩展 AI 能力。用户可根据转录文本快速生成粗剪，或一键应用 AI 特效，显著提升播客视频、教程录制等后期制作效率。",
        "es": "Palmier Pro is a macOS video editor designed to integrate AI directly into the editing workflow, solving the problem of manual, time-consuming video production. Its core strength lies in leveraging local AI models like Claude and Seedance2 for tasks such as scene detection, transcription, and automated editing, all while keeping data private on-device. You can use it to quickly generate rough cuts from transcripts or apply AI-powered effects, making it ideal for content creators who want to speed up post-production without leaving the desktop.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "palmier-pro stands out for ai-video, claude, and macos in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Palmier Pro is a macOS video editor designed to integrate AI directly into the editing workflow, solving the problem of manual, time-consuming video production. Its core strength lies in leveraging local AI models like Claude and Seedance2 for tasks such as scene detection, transcription, and automated editing, all while keeping data private on-device. You can use it to quickly generate rough cuts from transcripts or apply AI-powered effects, making it ideal for content creators who want to speed up post-production without leaving the desktop.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/palmier-io/palmier-pro for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
